 "phase": "W0 + W1: NTSDHeadless for wasm32-unknown-wasip1, every scenario under WASI",
 "change": "Core: a WASI clock (__wasi_clock_time_get, ids 0/1), OriginalConcurrentInputs.map without Dispatch (bodies in turn) and Background computed at creation on WASI, five size checks compared in 64 bits (Int(UInt32.max) traps with a 32-bit Int). Runtime: OriginalMainQueue (DispatchQueue.main as before; on WASI a timer list served by run() in deadline then creation order) for the session's iterations, the shell and playback delays and TouchMouse; an inline render executor and an immediate release on WASI; OriginalMacWinsock left out on WASI with OriginalUnavailableSockets; the display budget clamped (3<<30 wrapped negative); Data.writeReplacing (.atomic, or a plain write on WASI). Headless: the WASI sockets stub and OriginalMainQueue.run(). Tools: wasi_run.mjs (Node WASI runner) and run_headless_scenarios.py --wasi.",
 "review": "Independent review: OK, no defect; existing hosts run identical code paths. Low follow-ups (code-after-return warnings, a 32-bit timer counter, read-only preopens, node --disable-warning, recording the node version) and older code that traps on wasm32 where 64-bit hosts throw (OriginalWorldCPoints frame -6, OriginalReplayFileInput payload length with a high byte >= 0x80, ~60 Int(UInt32) table reads, BMP header words, Int overflows only reachable through corruption) are W1b.",
 "notes": "WASI build: swift-6.4.0-RELEASE_wasm with the open-source 6.4.0 toolchain, NTSDHeadless.wasm 96 MB (with debug info); Node 20.19.5's V8 crashed compiling it (GC fatal error), Node 26.7.0 runs it. All 10 scenarios under WASI equal to their references and all 18,088 frames and digests identical to the Mac headless run of this gate (the none group); vs also identical to m1-frames-ref. Load under WASI ~0.9 s against 0.33 s natively (single-threaded, JIT). Existing hosts: all 10 scenarios, AppKit, unchecked and emulator equal with frames identical; 12 suites; phone A/B (music and sounds) overlapping in load (5.28-6.17 against 5.59-5.60 s), launch to loaded, peak, PSS, render, process, audio and CPU since launch; main 10.82-10.84 against 10.74-10.80 ms per tick (the L20 warm-up run 10.84), no W0 change running per tick on Android (its host schedules iterations itself; the rest are WASI-only branches or load-time code).",
